home-eyebrow = Resource workspace
home-title = Bring PvZ resource work into one workspace.
home-description = Browse RSB, PAK, DZip and experimental BNK archives, create or apply RSBP patches, process SMF, Compiled Text and Crypt-Data, edit RTON, Particle and REANIM, preview PAM animation, convert WEM audio, maintain NEWTON manifests, and use independent Rust format libraries as needed. Each tool stays focused while the interface and workflow remain consistent.
home-open-tool = Open { $tool }
home-open-experimental-tool = Open { $tool } (experimental)
home-quick-access = Quick access
home-workspaces-title = Workspaces
home-workspaces-intro = Every tool keeps its specialist workflow while sharing one navigation system and visual language.
home-for-developers = For developers
home-libraries-title = Independent format libraries
home-libraries-intro = The app composes only the libraries it needs. Other projects can depend on one crate without pulling in the GUI or an aggregate SDK.
home-getting-started = Getting started
home-start-title = Start with a file
home-step-one-title = Choose a workspace
home-step-one-body = Use RSB, PAK and DZip for archives, SMF for zlib containers, Compiled Text and Crypt-Data for protected resources, experimental BNK for SoundBanks, RTON for data, PAM and REANIM for animation, Particle for effects, WEM for audio, and NEWTON for manifests.
home-step-two-title = Open or drop a file
home-step-two-body = Resources are read locally and no CLI is required.
home-step-three-title = Inspect, edit and export
home-step-three-body = Keep the original format or convert it to an open format.
home-growth-title = Ready for more formats
home-growth-body = Future tools can reuse the same shell while their libraries continue to ship independently.
home-footer = One app shell · Focused format libraries

tool-rsb-description = Browse and edit RSB/RSG like a desktop archive utility, preview PTX textures, and extract resources on demand.
tool-rsb-patch-description = Create, inspect and apply normalized RSBP/VCDIFF patches in stored or raw-packet form.
tool-pak-description = Browse and edit PopCap PAK archives across PC, Xbox 360 and TV ZIP containers.
tool-dzip-description = Browse, edit and create DZip or split archives with DZ, Zlib, BZip and LZMA per-file compression.
tool-smf-description = Detect and unpack PopCap SMF automatically, or wrap files with configurable zlib and 8/16-byte headers.
tool-compiled-text-description = Edit text and encode or decode PopCap Compiled Text with configurable Seed, Rijndael-192-CBC, Base64 and SMF options.
tool-crypt-data-description = Detect CRYPT_RES and encrypt or decrypt PopCap resource prefixes with configurable keys and ranges.
tool-rton-description = Open, search and edit standard or Compact RTON, then convert between structured text formats.
tool-pam-description = Preview animation, inspect images and sprites, and export binary, text, image or FLA/XFL output.
tool-particle-description = Inspect and edit Particle/Trail emitters, fields and tracks, with XML and multi-platform compiled conversion.
tool-reanim-description = Edit REANIM tracks and frame transforms, then convert structured text, XFL and multi-platform compiled layouts.
tool-wem-description = Play WEM and common audio, then convert between Wwise WEM, WAV, Ogg Vorbis and AAC.
tool-bnk-description = Browse and rewrite Wwise SoundBank BKHD/HIRC objects and embedded WEM, then validate and rebuild BNK.
tool-newton-description = Inspect and edit PvZ2 resource manifests, with conversion between NEWTON, JSON, YAML and TOML.
