libraries-kicker = Developer libraries
libraries-title = Independent Rust libraries designed around each format
libraries-intro = Each format library keeps its own repository, version and public API. The app composes only what its workflows need, while other developers can select individual libraries directly.
libraries-toolkit-github = Toolkit on GitHub
libraries-summary-label = Library overview
libraries-independent-repositories = Independent repositories
libraries-typed-apis = Typed public APIs
libraries-depend-only = Depend only on what you use
libraries-format-crates = Format crates
libraries-section-title = Choose the format capabilities you need
libraries-repository-count = { $count } repositories
libraries-section-intro = Each card opens its GitHub repository in a new window. README files, public APIs, release history and workflows are maintained independently.
libraries-principle-release-title = Independent releases
libraries-principle-release-body = Each library owns its repository and history, and can be tested, tagged and consumed independently.
libraries-principle-compose-title = Compose on demand
libraries-principle-compose-body = There is no aggregate SDK; archive, data, animation and audio capabilities can be selected separately.
libraries-principle-gui-title = GUI decoupled
libraries-principle-gui-body = Format crates do not depend on the Toolkit UI and can be used in desktop, Web, service or custom tooling.
libraries-footer = Independent histories · Focused APIs · Shared workspace

library-rsb-archive-summary = RSB/RSG archives, zlib and PTX texture codecs
library-rsb-archive-overview = Read, validate and rebuild RSB/RSG archives with zlib streams and PTX texture codecs.
library-rsb-patch-summary = RSBP containers and standard/interleaved VCDIFF patches
library-rsb-patch-overview = Create and apply RSBP patches across stored, raw-packet and standard or interleaved VCDIFF data.
library-pak-archive-summary = PopCap PAK, XOR variants, zlib and TV ZIP containers
library-pak-archive-overview = Handle PopCap PAK platform byte order, XOR variants, zlib data and TV ZIP containers.
library-dzip-archive-summary = DZip, split volumes and DZ/Zlib/BZip/LZMA codecs
library-dzip-archive-overview = Read and build DZip or split archives with integrated DZ, Zlib, BZip and LZMA pipelines.
library-smf-container-summary = SMF auto-detection, zlib streaming and MD5 tag sidecars
library-smf-container-overview = Detect PopCap SMF variants and provide streaming zlib unpacking, wrapping and MD5 tag handling.
library-serde-rton-summary = Serde reader, writer, Value and crypto helpers
library-serde-rton-overview = Read and write standard or Compact RTON with a Serde-style API, Value model and optional crypto.
library-pam-codec-summary = Typed PAM binary decoding and encoding
library-pam-codec-overview = Decode and encode PAM animation, image, sprite and per-frame commands with typed models.
library-particle-codec-summary = Particle and Trail binary/XML codecs
library-particle-codec-overview = Handle Particle and Trail emitters, fields, tracks and XML/compiled round trips.
library-reanim-codec-summary = REANIM timeline, transform, compiled and XFL codecs
library-reanim-codec-overview = Parse REANIM timelines and transforms with multi-platform compiled layouts and XFL conversion.
library-wem-audio-summary = Wwise WEM inspection, playback decoding and audio encoding
library-wem-audio-overview = Inspect Wwise WEM, decode audio for playback, and convert among WEM, WAV, Ogg Vorbis and AAC.
library-bnk-archive-summary = Wwise SoundBank chunks, HIRC objects and embedded WEM
library-bnk-archive-overview = Parse and rebuild Wwise SoundBank chunks, HIRC objects and embedded WEM media.
library-compiled-text-summary = Base64 and Rijndael-192-CBC PopCap text containers
library-compiled-text-overview = Read and write PopCap compiled-text protected by Base64 and Rijndael-192-CBC.
library-crypt-data-summary = CRYPT_RES headers and configurable prefix XOR
library-crypt-data-overview = Detect CRYPT_RES headers and process PopCap prefix XOR with configurable keys and ranges.
library-newton-manifest-summary = PvZ2 manifest groups, slots and atlas metadata
library-newton-manifest-overview = Read and write PvZ2 NEWTON manifests, resource groups, slots, subgroup references and atlas metadata.

about-kicker = About
about-title = About Ed1th's PvZ Toolkit
about-intro = An open-source workspace for PopCap and PvZ resource formats. Archive browsing, RSBP patches, SMF compression, Compiled Text and Crypt-Data protection, RTON data, Particle and REANIM editing, PAM animation, WEM audio, NEWTON manifests and reusable format libraries share one coherent experience.
about-mission-title = Open, focused and local-first
about-mission-kicker = Built for format tooling
about-mission-body-one = Toolkit combines specialist tools in one application shell while keeping its archive, data, animation, audio and security crates independent, testable and directly reusable by other Rust projects.
about-mission-body-two = Files are processed locally. Web and desktop share the same workflows without requiring a CLI or aggregate SDK.
about-principle-local = Local processing
about-principle-libraries = Independent libraries
about-principle-workspace = One workspace
